; The near-misses an editor has to be able to talk about. `not_member` is
; already pinned for a wrong magnitude and a wrong single-letter unit
; (`digit-leading-member-not-member`); these are the three shapes a typo
; actually takes when the member spelling is longer than one letter.
;
;   * `2dd` — a doubled letter. The unit is `dd`, one edit from `d`.
;   * `2d-arry` — a hyphenated unit one edit from `d-array`. It is one
;     token only because a `-` may join two letter runs inside a unit, so
;     a typo inside the second run stays one token too.
;   * `2.5d` — a fractional magnitude, which no spelling can be at all:
;     `2d`, `2.0d` and `02d` are one member and `2.5d` is none of them.
;
; All three report `not_member` rather than `wrong_underlying`: once the
; kind declares a digit-leading member the slot genuinely accepts
; unit-bearing numbers, so "which ones are allowed" is the useful report.
(plugin :name gpu :version "1.0.0"
  (value-kind :name view-dimension :underlying symbol
    :members (member-set :values [1d 2d 2d-array cube 3d]))
  (form :name texture (key :name view :type view-dimension)))

(texture :view 2dd)
(texture :view 2d-arry)
(texture :view 2.5d)
